ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: retention.seq.stack-delete
display_id: SEQ-RETENTION-STACK-DELETE
module: retention
title: Delete a whole stack
summary: Removes a stack's directory and registry entry after the owner confirms, and queues the cloud
  copy's deletion when the owner asks.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: call
  text: The owner deletes a stack
participants:
- actor.owner
- sys.daemon
- id: db
  is:
  - sys.home
  label: Stack database
- id: registry
  is:
  - sys.home
  label: Registry database
- id: dir
  is:
  - sys.home
  label: Stack directory
items:
- msg:
    from: actor.owner
    to: sys.daemon
    text: Delete this stack
    inputs:
    - name: stack_id
      source: The owner's command
      source_kind: parameter
- alt:
    branches:
    - when: the request does not come from an interactive terminal
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: actor.owner
          text: Refuse; deleting a stack needs a terminal
          reply: true
          results:
          - code: needs_terminal
    - when: the owner is at an interactive terminal
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: actor.owner
          text: Show the stack's memory counts, whether it syncs, and ask to confirm
          results:
          - copy: Delete {stack} and its {count} memories permanently? Type the stack name to confirm.
      - opt:
          when: the stack syncs to the cloud and the owner asks to delete the cloud copy too
          items:
          - msg:
              from: sys.daemon
              to: db
              text: Queue the cloud deletion of the whole stack
              ops:
              - op: enqueue
                entity: sync.data.sync-queue
                set:
                - change = stack_deleted
                - state = pending
          - msg:
              from: sys.daemon
              to: sys.daemon
              text: Push the deletion before removing local files
              invokes:
              - sync.seq.sync
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Stop the stack's runs and remove its projected skills
          note: Waits for any running maintenance run on the stack to finish
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: dir
          text: Remove the stack directory recursively, with its database and its log files
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: registry
          text: Remove the stack from the registry
          ops:
          - op: delete
            entity: stacks.data.stack
            by:
            - stack_id
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: actor.owner
          text: Deleted
          reply: true
rationale: Removing the whole directory leaves nothing behind in database pages, which row deletion cannot
  promise. A stack that syncs pushes its deletion first, so the next sync from another device does not
  bring it back.
